of some books before either a) the doctors burned them; or b) the
government seized them.

My second is that there are magazines and books on survivalism and
self-sufficiency that probably go beyond the first-aid level, and it
might be a good idea to get some back issues before they ran out.

My third is that a veterinarian might be helpful, either for
rudimentary training or for pointers to information or both.

Fourth -- doing it the hard way, quite a bit could probably be gleaned
by careful study of an encyclopedia.

Fifth -- find an herbalist, and other sources on folk remedies; many
of them actually do work.

